<section class="section">
 <div class="container">
 <h2 class="section-title">Clinical standards you can verify.</h2>
 <div class="grid grid--3">
 <div class="card card--soft"><h3>Credentialed RNs</h3><p>Care is delivered by credentialed local nursing partners who live and work in your patient's community. Every nurse must clear CoreFlow's credentialing and competency requirements before taking an assignment, and every visit is supervised under our clinical protocols.</p></div>
 <div class="card card--soft"><h3>SC Board of Pharmacy (state licensure)</h3><p>{{ site.legalEntity }} holds {{ site.permitAuthority }} permit #{{ site.permitNumber }}, active and in good standing. Permit documentation is available to your office on request. State licensure is separate from accreditation.</p></div>
 <div class="card card--soft"><h3>URAC &amp; ACHC (pursuing)</h3><p>Actively pursuing URAC Specialty Pharmacy v5.0 and ACHC IRX-NO797, anticipated Q4 2026. Accreditation has been initiated and has not yet been awarded.</p></div>
 <div class="card card--soft"><h3>Cold chain</h3><p>Commercially manufactured, pre-compounded medications. USP 659/1079 cold chain. Temperature-monitored storage and delivery.</p></div>
 <div class="card card--soft"><h3>Documentation</h3><p>Clinical notes returned to your office after every visit. Made available to payer UM for PA and concurrent review.</p></div>
 <div class="card card--soft"><h3>Non-compounding</h3><p>CoreFlow does not perform sterile compounding. All medications are received as commercially manufactured products.</p></div>
 </div>
 </div>
</section>

